{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-32","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：整数","englishTitle":"Each of the numbers which are continually doubled beginning from a dyad is even-times even only.","book":9,"number":32,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":32,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","contentId":"euclid-9-32","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"47f3308a0dc10ae53b63365fdfc3b5b75167e1a768a9348fa5c0d80a157873d4","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-32.statement","euclid-9-32.construction.1","euclid-9-32.proof.1","euclid-9-32.proof.2","euclid-9-32.construction.2","euclid-9-32.proof.3","euclid-9-32.proof.4","euclid-9-32.conclusion","euclid-9-32.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-32.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"40f183ec9e375f84cc409ae383252d359752ded0689b1ef6bb74de939c591cf6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Each of the numbers which are continually doubled beginning from a dyad is even-times even only."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从一个阴道开始,每个数字不断翻一番,都是偶数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"34a5b8d99e4aa8eb9237bebbaf478e56c7160ad2a8dfa694784cfed3525844b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let as many numbers as we please, B, C, D, have been continually doubled beginning from the dyad A; I say that B, C, D are eventimes even only."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"B,C,D,从A公元开始,不断翻一番。 我说,B,C,D甚至只是偶数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"fa0a41ecf8a70c5d1d3944d5eab9a124f2da15d4e117b2beb035f989e6f16150","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now that each of the numbers B, C, D is even-times even is manifest; for it is doubled from a dyad."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,B,C,D数字中的每一个数字甚至都是偶数,因为数字从一个山顶上翻了一倍。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"62c66b656901a03f6a954b8bc4295fcaad2a2a051cb0c200bf82e032ad5d882f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say that it is also even-times even only."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"我说,这甚至只是偶数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":4,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"225b9980badfd7df4b703d96991fe7e705d945543503c49574a9e267184a0bb8","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let an unit be set out."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"准备单位"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b8d110a12fc8b350d1aa91153345d64ee64308adbad8ea32f80a0d5cb1cbbc56","citations":["euclid-9-13"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then as many numbers as we please beginning from an unit are in continued proportion, and the number A after the unit is prime, therefore D, the greatest of the numbers A, B, C, D, will not be measured by any other number except A, B, C. [[IX. 13](/principles/euclid-9-13)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从那时起,我们想从单位开始的人数是连比例,单位之后的数字是A,因此,D,D中最多的数字是A、B、C、D,除A、B、C外,将不以任何其他数字来整除。 [[IX. 13](/principles/euclid-9-13)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"61b9c5775d4c95f62841347a19f06c8b72c10f686a62ede70a84d4bbfb91b8c4","citations":["euclid-7-def-8"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And each of the numbers A, B, C is even; therefore D is even-times even only. [[VII. Def. 8](/principles/euclid-7-def-8)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A,B,C数字都是平的, 所以D数字甚至只是偶数。 [[VII. Def. 8](/principles/euclid-7-def-8)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":7,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"079c09e311d15654b061292b541af3413d4c0866286dbbf435836309c89b3383","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that each of the numbers B, C is even-times even only. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们也可以证明,B,C数字中的每一个数字都是偶数,甚至只有Q,E,D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-32.source","contentId":"euclid-9-32","revisionId":"euclid-9-32@raw-47f3308a0dc10ae5","order":8,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1b4186add84c49711786563989abacf9107c06ff49a8f4865f4275790d7ab2e5","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-9-32:euclid-9-13:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-32","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-32.proof.3"],"targetContentId":"euclid-9-13","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32/","sourceLabel":"IX. 13"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-9-32:euclid-7-def-8:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-9-32","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-9-32.proof.4"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-def-8","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.32/","sourceLabel":"VII. Def. 8"}}],"incomingEdges":[],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-9-32:euclid-9-13:explicit","id":"euclid-9-13","book":9,"number":13,"kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：连比例与比例与整数","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"},{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-9-32:euclid-7-def-8:explicit","id":"euclid-7-def-8","book":7,"number":8,"kind":"definition","title":"偶乘偶数","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-number","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
